.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-REVOKE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-revoke - Disconnect and revoke a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine revoke <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Disconnect and revoke a machine

.PP
Disconnect and revoke the selected enrollment. Existing machine credentials lose authority; the confirmation code confirms this account-level removal.

.PP
Machines are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected machine, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
